Loading a process's image clears every entry past it up to the end of those that grant user mode a right,
the fence among them, which leaves the core's hardwired entries open to the process.

Caught-by: fuzz-rp2350
Report: PMP CSRs grant rights the slots do not

diff --git a/kernel/process.c b/kernel/process.c
--- a/kernel/process.c
+++ b/kernel/process.c
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ void process_activate(struct process *proc)
         LOOP_BOUND(PROCESS_REGION_SLOTS);
         pmp_set(i, img->addr[i], img->cfg[i]);
     }
-    for (unsigned i = img->count; i < pmp_entry_count; i++) {
+    for (unsigned i = img->count; i < pmp_entry_end; i++) {
         LOOP_BOUND(PMP_MAX_ENTRIES);
         pmp_clear(i);
     }
